EightlyEighthly, if you would not be taken with any of SatansSatan's ſnaressnares, and devices, then keep up your communion with God; your ſtrengthstrength to ſtandstand, and withſtandwithstand 2 Cor. 6. 16. The words are very ſignificantsignificant in the original, there are two ins, as if God could never have nearenear enough communion with them. SatansSatan's fiery darts, is from your communion with God; a ſoulsoul high in communion with God may be tempted, but will not eaſilyeasily be conque • red, ſuchsuch a ſoulsoul wilwill fight it out to the death; Communioncommunion with God furniſhethfurnisheth the ſoulesoul with the greateſtgreatest, and the choiſeſtchoicest arguments to withſtandwithstand SatansSatan's temptations;
Communioncommunion is the reſultresult of union; communion is a reciprocallreciprocal exchange between ChriſtChrist, and a gracious ſoulesoul; Communioncommunion is JacobsJacob's ladder, where you have ChriſtChrist ſweetlysweetly coming down into the ſoulsoul, and the ſoulsoul by divine influences ſweetlysweetly aſcendingascending up to ChriſtChrist. Communion with ChriſtChrist is very inflaming, raiſingraising, and ſtrengthningstrengtheningstrengthning; while SampſonSamson kept up his communionThe ſeasea ebbs and flows, the Moon encreaſesincreasesencreases, and decreaſesdecreases, ſoso 'tis’tis with Saints in their communion with God. with God, no enemy could ſtandstand before him, but he goes on conquering, and to conquer; but when he was fallen in his communion with God, he quickly falls before the plots of his enemies; 'twil’twill be ſoso with your ſoulessouls, ſoso long as your communion with God is kept up, you wilwill be too hard for ſpiritualspiritual wickedneſſeswickedness in high places; but if you fall from your Plutarch tells of Eudoxus, that he would be willing to be burnt up preſentlypresently by the Sun, ſoso he might be admitted to come ſoso near it, as to learnelearn the nature of it; what ſhouldshould not weewe be content to ſuffersuffer for the keeping up of commuioncommunion with ChriſtChrist? communion with God, you will fall as others before the face of every temptation. David, ſoso long as he kept up his communion with God, he ſtandsstands, and triumphs over all his enemies; but when he was fallen in his communion with God, then he falls before the enemies, that were in his own boſombosom, & flies before thoſethose that purſuedpursued after his life; 'Twil’twill be ſoso with your ſoulssouls, if you doedo not keepekeep up your communion with God. IobJob keeps up his communion with God, and conquers Satan upon the dunghill.
Adam looſesloseslooses his communion with God, and is conquered by Satan in ParadiſeParadise. Communion with God is a ſhieldshield upon land, as well as an anchor at ſeasea; 'tis’tis a ſwordsword to defend you, as well as a ſtaffestaff to ſupportsupport you; therefore keep up your communion.
